## [0002] Arvig brand palette extracted from source

**Decision:** colors were sampled from the live stylesheet at https://arvig.com/
rather than eyeballed from screenshots.

| Token | Hex | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--color-arvig-700` | `#1D1060` | Official Arvig deep indigo — primary buttons, headings, dark sections |
| `--color-lime-brand` | `#C0D52F` | Official Arvig lime — accents, badges, accent CTA |
| `--color-teal-brand` | `#31CDCF` | Secondary accent from the same sheet |
| `--color-ink` | `#313131` | Body charcoal |
| `--color-ink-mute` | `#7A7A82` | Muted type, cents, fine print |
| `--color-canvas-alt` | `#F7F7FB` | Alternating section tint |

A 50–950 ramp was interpolated around `#1D1060` so hover, border and tint
states stay on-brand. `#1D1060` and `#C0D52F` are used verbatim.

**Files:** `app/globals.css`

**Revert:** replace the `@theme` block; no component hard-codes a hex value.

---

## [0003] Centralized data architecture — `lib/content.ts`

**Core requirement.** One file is the single source of truth for every price,
speed, feature list, disclosure line and CTA label.

- `PlanItem` interface implemented exactly as specified, plus five optional
  presentation fields (`tagline`, `speedLabel`, `priceNote`, `priceUnit`,
  `bestFor`) so cards stay expressive without layout files holding data.
- `plans[]` holds all 14 plans across six service lines.
- `serviceSections[]` declares the canonical order:
  **fiber → cable → bundle → tv → mobile → phone**.
- Derived selectors — `plansFor()`, `getPlan()`, `activeSections`,
  `lowestPrice()`, `speedLabel()`, `finePrintRows()`, `ctaLabelFor()` — are the
  only way layouts read data. No TSX file touches the `plans` array directly.
- `activeSections` filters out any service line with zero plans, which makes an
  empty placeholder section structurally impossible.

**Cascade guarantee:** editing a `price` in this file updates the hero anchor,
the plan card, the fine-print grid row and the CTA label simultaneously,
because all four read the same `PlanItem`.

**Files:** `lib/content.ts`

**Revert:** this file is the only place plan data lives; restoring a prior copy
fully restores prior pricing.

