## [0005] Universal `<PriceLockup plan={plan} />`

One component renders every price on the site: a flex row of dollar sign,
dominant integer (2.1rem / 2.75rem / 3.4rem by `size`), and muted cents, with
the unit (`/mo`, `/mo per line`) pulled from the plan.

- Used by the hero anchor (`size="lg" tone="dark"`), every plan card
  (`size="md"`) and the fine-print grid's derived monthly string.
- When `plan.price` is undefined it falls back to `plan.priceNote` instead of
  rendering an empty lockup — the same condition that flips the CTA to
  "Call for pricing".
- Carries an `sr-only` sentence so screen readers hear one clean price rather
  than the visually split integer and cents.

**Files:** `components/PriceLockup.tsx`

---

## [0006] Component layer

| Component | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `TopChrome` | Non-dismissable disclosure bar + sticky header, mobile nav |
| `Wordmark` | Type-set Arvig wordmark with lime dot; no image request |
| `Hero` | Headline, subline, price anchor, ZIP checker **and** call button, trust chips |
| `PlanCard` | One card; CTA label derived by `ctaLabelFor()` |
| `ServiceSection` | Renders any service line from a `ServiceSection` record |
| `FinePrintGrid` | `<table>` from `md` up, stacked cards below |
| `HowItWorks` | Three-step process + six-item "why order here" grid |
| `Faq` | Native `<details>`/`<summary>` accordion, zero runtime JS |
| `Footer` | Dark footer matching the bestfiberinternet.us structure |
| `CallCta` | **The only** place a `tel:` link is built — guarantees `data-call-cta` |
| `Reveal` | One-shot IntersectionObserver entrance |
| `SmoothScroll` | Lenis setup + anchor interception with header offset |

**Architectural note:** `CallCta` is deliberately the sole constructor of
`tel:` hrefs. Every call-to-action therefore carries `data-call-cta="<surface>"`
by construction rather than by convention, so the attribute cannot be dropped
by a future edit.

**Files:** `components/*.tsx`, `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`

---

## [0007] Motion policy

**Kept:** Lenis smooth scroll (duration 1.05, exponential ease), one-shot
fade-and-lift reveals with a 40–80 ms stagger, card hover lift of 3 px, button
hover/active states, accordion chevron rotation.

**Deliberately excluded:** WebGL, 3D spiral hero backgrounds, animated assembly
diagrams, parallax, scroll-jacked section pinning, looping animations.

Lenis is skipped outright when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set, and
`globals.css` neutralizes reveals and transitions under the same query.

**Files:** `components/SmoothScroll.tsx`, `components/Reveal.tsx`,
`app/globals.css`

---

## [0008] Negative-constraint compliance

Enforced structurally where possible rather than by review:

- **Support routing** — no copy anywhere directs customers to contact Arvig for
  billing, outages or support. All CTAs route to the retailer sales line.
- **Hero call button** — retained alongside the ZIP checker.
- **CTA text** — `ctaLabelFor()` returns only "Call to order" or
  "Call for pricing". The raw phone number appears as a label in exactly two
  places, the header and the footer contact column.
- **No competitor bashing / no self-deprecating copy** — the banned phrasings do
  not appear; cable and fiber are described on their own merits.
- **No empty sections** — `activeSections` filters zero-plan service lines out.
- **No Broadband Facts label links** — none present.
- **No date stamps** — no "Pricing observed …" string exists. (Note: the footer
  reference site carries one; it was intentionally not reproduced.)
- **No "is this the official site" FAQ** — the eight FAQ entries cover speeds,
  data caps, installation, service requirements, bundling, Managed WiFi,
  "starting at" pricing and number portability.
- **Footer** — matches the reference structure: brand column + blurb, two link
  columns, contact column with number and hours, full-width legal block,
  bottom bar with policy links and copyright.

