## [0011] Hero redesign — panel removed, ZIP-only conversion path

**Request:** the hero's right-hand card read as a generic template. Referenced
kineticfiber.us and bestfiberinternet.us.

**What the references actually do:** both run a **single-column hero with no
boxed panel**. bestfiberinternet.us stacks headline → paragraph → "See what's
available at your address" → ZIP input + Check availability → microcopy.
kineticfiber.us is headline → subheading → price callout → CTA, described as a
"clean text-based design without boxed panels". The glassy card was the
template tell, so it is gone.

**Changes to `components/Hero.tsx`:**
- Split two-column grid → one centered column, `max-w-[900px]`.
- Removed the `rounded-[20px] border bg-white/[0.06]` panel entirely.
- ZIP form rebuilt as a **fused search pill**: one white `rounded-full`
  container with `p-1.5`, transparent input on the left, solid lime button
  inset on the right, `0 20px 50px -22px` drop shadow and a 1px ring.
  Below `sm` it unfuses into two stacked full-width controls, so the
  320px layout keeps exact 20px gutters.
- Focus handling follows the pill: `focus-within` ring on the container at
  `sm`+, `focus-visible` ring on the bare input below that.
- Background wash rebalanced to three centered blurs for a symmetric column.
- H1 `max-w` raised to `21ch` at `sm`+ so "high-speed" stops breaking mid-word;
  now sets in three balanced lines.
- Price-anchor detail block drops its `border-l` and left padding and centres
  once it wraps below the price (`sm:border-l sm:pl-6 sm:text-left`).

**Hero call CTA removed — deliberate override of the earlier boss rule.**
The original spec said "Do NOT remove the call button from the hero." When the
conflict was raised the instruction was: *"remove the call to order button.
include only zipcode and check availability button."* So the hero now carries
**no phone CTA at all** — no button, no "Speak with a retail specialist" line,
no number in the ZIP success message. The sticky header's call button sits
directly above the hero and still holds the number on screen.

To restore it, add a `<CallCta location="hero">` below the form and re-import
`CallCta` in `components/Hero.tsx`.

**Changes to `lib/content.ts`:**
- `anchorLabel`: "Fiber internet starting at" → "Fiber plans start at".
- Added `zipInvalid` and `zipSuccess` so the form's messages live in the data
  file like everything else. `zipSuccess` no longer mentions the phone number.

**Verification:** hero contains **0** `tel:` links, no phone number and no
"call" string. Sitewide tel links 20 → 19, still **0 missing `data-call-cta`**.
Pill measured fused at desktop (560px, centred, button inset, shadow applied)
and `flex-direction: column` at 320px with both controls spanning 20→300.
**0 gutter violations** page-wide at 320px; no horizontal scroll.
`tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` static at 7.93 kB / 110 kB.

