## [0013] Palette locked to Arvig's exact shades + professional copy pass

### Colors

Sampled from arvig.com's **own CSS declarations** (`curl` + grep over the
served HTML), not from screenshots:

| Hex | Evidence on arvig.com |
| --- | --- |
| `#1D1060` | `color:` x26, `background-color:` x5 — the primary |
| `#C0D52F` | `background-color:` x2 — the button accent |
| `#F8F8F8` | section tint |
| `#A0A0A0` | `color:` x3 — muted text |
| `#313131` | body charcoal |

**Removed:** the interpolated purple-leaning indigo ramp (`#f5f4fb`, `#eae7f6`,
`#d2ccec`, `#aea3dc`, `#8574c8`, `#5c47ad`, `#3d2a8c`) and the invented teal
(`#31CDCF`, `#1B9799`). The teal appeared only in a WordPress preset block, not
in any Arvig brand rule, so it was never an Arvig color.

**Now:** every hex in `app/globals.css` is either an official color used
verbatim or a straight mix of one with white or black. No new hues:

- `#170D4F` = `#1D1060` + 18% black (footer)
- `#1A0E56` = `#1D1060` + 10% black (button hover)
- `#A59FBF` / `#CDCADC` / `#E8E7EF` / `#F4F3F7` = 40/22/10/5% `#1D1060` on white
- `#CCDD59` = `#C0D52F` + 20% white · `#A3B528` = `#C0D52F` + 15% black
- `#5A5A5A` = `#313131` + 20% white
- `#6F6F6F` = `#A0A0A0` + 30% black — darkened only so small print clears
  WCAG AA; `#A0A0A0` itself is 2.8:1 on white and fails for body text
- `#DEDEDE` / `#EEEEEE` = 35/18% `#A0A0A0` on white (borders)

Hero background washes changed from a teal blur to white and lime at low alpha,
keeping the whole page inside Arvig's palette.

Rendered values confirmed in-browser: hero `#1d1060`, primary button `#1d1060`,
accent button `#c0d52f`, tinted section `#f8f8f8`, headings `#1d1060`.

### Copy — professional pass on seven sections

| Section | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Cable | "Cable internet where fiber is still on the way" | "Cable internet across the Arvig service area" |
| Bundles | "Put the household on one account" | "Bundled services on a single account" |
| TV | "Arvig TV, delivered over your connection" | "Television delivered over your Arvig connection" |
| Mobile | "Mobile lines that ride on your home account" | "Mobile service on your Arvig account" |
| Phone | "A landline that still makes sense" | "Dependable home phone service" |
| Fine print | "What each plan actually costs to run" | "Complete pricing and plan terms" |
| Why us | "Straight answers before you sign up" | "What sets Arvig service apart" |

Each section's intro paragraph was rewritten alongside its heading, replacing
colloquial verbs ("rides on", "attach to it", "set out beside") with plain
professional phrasing. No factual claim changed — speeds, rates, the Arvig
internet requirement for TV and Mobile, and the unlimited-data policy are all
as previously sourced.

**Files:** `app/globals.css`, `components/Hero.tsx`, `lib/content.ts`

