## [0014] Photography added — 7 images

Images were supplied as **PNG, 1408x768, 28.9 MB total** (3.4-5.5 MB each).
Two problems had to be fixed before they could ship.

### 1. Weight — 28.9 MB to 0.92 MB

Re-encoded to progressive mozjpeg at q82 via `sharp`. PNG originals moved to
`assets-source/` at the project root, **outside `public/`**, so they are never
served. That folder is ~30 MB; it is the only copy of the uncropped originals,
so it was kept rather than deleted, but it should probably stay out of git.

### 2. Gemini watermark — removed by crop

Every image carried Gemini's visible four-pointed sparkle watermark in the
bottom-right, located at **x 1265-1310, y 620-665** of 1408x768. On a page whose
whole point is not looking AI-generated, that mark is the giveaway.

Fixed by re-cutting from the PNG originals with `extract({width:1250})` — the
right 11%, which starts before the watermark at x=1265. Final images are
**1250x768**. Verified by compositing all seven bottom-right corners into one
contact sheet: no mark on any of them.

Final shipped weight: **884 KB across 7 files.**

### Placement rule

Imagery is data-driven. `SectionImage { src, alt, layout }` was added to
`lib/content.ts`, and `ServiceSection.tsx` reads it — no layout file holds a
file path.

| Layout | Applies to | Rendering |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `side` | sections with <= 2 plans (cable, TV, phone) | image and cards share a row from `lg`, `0.82fr / 1.18fr` |
| `banner` | sections with 3 plans (mobile) | full-width strip above the cards |
| none | fiber, bundles | already three cards wide; images there would make the page image-soup |

| Image | Placement |
| --- | --- |
| `hero-home-fiber.jpg` | Full-bleed hero backdrop, `priority` |
| `install-technician.jpg` | How It Works — split; the 3-across step grid became image + stacked steps |
| `why-us-local-team.jpg` | Why Us — wide band under the heading |
| `cable-neighborhood.jpg` | Cable — side |
| `tv-living-room.jpg` | TV — side |
| `home-phone-kitchen.jpg` | Phone — side |
| `mobile-everyday.jpg` | Mobile — banner |

### Hero scrim

First attempt stacked `bg-arvig-900/80` **and** a `/75 -> /70 -> /95` gradient.
Those multiply: `1 - (0.2 x 0.3)` = **94% opaque**, which buried the photograph
entirely — the farmhouse was invisible.

Replaced with a single bottom-heavy gradient, `from-arvig-900/55 via/72
to-arvig-900/92`. Bottom-heavy so the ZIP row and trust chips sit on the
densest part. Worst case behind type is the lit windows (~235,185,125) under
the 72% mid stop: composite `#4a3566`, white on it ~9.3:1 and lime ~6.5:1, both
clear of AA.

### Verification

- 7 `<img>` in the server-rendered HTML; **6 `loading="lazy"`**, hero excluded
  and carrying a `rel="preload"` (how Next 15 implements `priority`).
- Correct `sizes` per placement; 8 srcset candidates each.
- At **320px**: no horizontal scroll, **0 gutter violations**, every section
  image measured exactly 280px wide inside the 20px gutters.
- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` static, 13.8 kB / 116 kB First Load JS.

