## [0015] Image treatment revisions

Five changes off the back of a review of the rendered page.

### Hero scrim lightened again

`from-arvig-900/55 via/72 to/92` was still too dense — the farmhouse read as a
vague silhouette. Now **`/38 -> /55 -> /85`**. Contrast recomputed for the worst
case, the lit windows (~235,185,125) under the 55% mid stop: composite
`#7a5c6d`, white on it ≈ **5.9:1**, still clear of AA for normal text. The
headline itself sits over the dusk sky, where contrast is far higher.

### New `background` image layout — cable and home phone

Added `layout: 'background'` to `SectionImage`. The photograph fills the whole
section edge to edge with **no scrim at all**, as asked.

Legibility is handled without dimming the picture: the eyebrow, heading and
intro move onto an opaque white panel (`bg-white/97`), and the plan cards were
already opaque white. So the image runs at full strength everywhere it is
visible, and no text is ever set directly on photography.

A `background` section also opts out of the alternating white / off-white
rhythm, since it supplies its own surface.

### Content held to the left on background sections

First attempt spread the panel and cards across the full width, which hid the
subject of both photographs behind the cards — the man on the phone was
completely covered. Content is now capped at **`lg:max-w-[62%]`**, leaving the
right of the frame clear. That is where the subject sits in both images.

`objectPosition` was added to `SectionImage` for per-image crop control:
- cable — `center 55%` (drops empty sky, keeps the street and pole)
- phone — `68% center` (holds the man in frame)

### Arvig Mobile banner — subject was decapitated

The banner cropped the woman's head. At 945px wide the image scales to 580px
tall; cropping 340px from centre removed 120px top, cutting into her hair at
y≈60. Fixed with **`objectPosition: 'center 18%'`**, biasing the crop window
upward so the top of the frame is preserved.

### Why Us copy cut back

Six two-to-three-sentence bodies reduced to one short line each, e.g.
"Arvig operates a 9,000 square-mile network across more than half of
Minnesota's counties, with high-capacity fiber routes through St. Cloud,
Rochester and the Twin Cities." -> "A 9,000 square-mile network reaching more
than half of Minnesota's counties." Titles and the six claims are unchanged.

### Verification

- At **320px**: no horizontal scroll, **0 gutter violations**; both background
  sections measured 320px wide with their `objectPosition` applied.
- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` static.

