## [0021] Why Us refined — split instead of overlay

The full-bleed treatment from [0019] did not work for this section and was
replaced.

### Why the overlay failed here

The cable and home phone photographs are wide, quiet scenes — a street, a
kitchen — so copy can sit over them. `why-us-local-team.jpg` is the opposite:
two people, mid-frame, in high-visibility vests. Laying a six-card grid across
it produced two problems at once. The subjects were buried behind the cards,
and the card copy sat over faces and vests, which no amount of scrim or card
opacity fixes. The two elements were competing for the same region of the
frame.

It is worth naming the general rule: a photograph works as a backdrop when its
subject is *not* where the content goes. Six cards occupy the whole width, so
only a photograph with no central subject can survive underneath them.

### What replaced it

A split. The picture gets its own slab, the copy gets a solid surface, and
neither sits on the other.

- `lg:grid-cols-[42%_58%]` — photograph left, claims right.
- The image carries only a light `bg-arvig-900/20` tint now, since no text
  sits on it. It reads as a photograph again rather than as texture.
- A gradient blend on the join (right edge at `lg`, bottom edge below that) so
  the two halves meet softly instead of at a hard seam.
- **Card chrome dropped entirely.** On solid indigo the claims need no panels:
  a 3px lime rule, the title, the body, and spacing do the separating. Six
  bordered translucent boxes were most of what made the old version look busy.
- Eyebrow returns to lime — on solid `#1D1060` it measures 9.9:1, so the
  contrast problem that forced it white over photography does not apply.

### Measurements

| | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Grid at 1385px | 581.5px photo / 803.1px content |
| Claim columns | 2 (left edges 646, 1003) |
| Section height | 695px, down from a much taller stack |
| Text contrast | white 16:1, arvig-100 13:1 on solid `#1D1060` |

At **320px** the grid collapses to one column: photograph 320x260 on top,
claims below, no horizontal scroll and **0 gutter violations**.

`tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` static.

