## [0023] Security patch — CVE-2025-66478 (React2Shell)

Vercel's first deployment built successfully but emitted:

```
npm warn deprecated next@15.5.4: This version has a security vulnerability.
Vulnerable version of Next.js detected, please update immediately.
```

### What it is

**CVE-2025-66478, CVSS 10.0, remote code execution.** A flaw in the React
Server Components protocol lets untrusted input influence server-side
execution. It originates upstream in React as CVE-2025-55182 ("React2Shell");
the Next.js advisory tracks the downstream impact on App Router apps.

Affected: Next.js 15.x and 16.x using RSC with the App Router. Not affected:
13.x, stable 14.x, Pages Router, Edge Runtime. **This project is squarely in
the affected set** — 15.5.4, App Router, RSC.

There is no workaround. Upgrading is the only fix.

### Upgrade

| Package | Was | Now | Patched from |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `next` | 15.5.4 | **15.5.25** | 15.5.7 |
| `react` | 19.1.1 | **19.1.9** | 19.1.2 |
| `react-dom` | 19.1.1 | **19.1.9** | 19.1.2 |

Upgrading Next alone is sufficient for App Router apps, since a patched React
is bundled inside the release. But the project's own `react`/`react-dom` sat at
19.1.1, one release below the 19.1.2 fix, so both were moved up as well rather
than left on a known-vulnerable version. Stayed inside the 15.5 and 19.1 lines
to keep the change surface small; caret ranges mean future patches in those
lines are picked up.

### Secret rotation — not required

The advisory recommends rotating application secrets for anything that was
online and unpatched. **This app has no environment variables and no secrets of
any kind**, so there is nothing to rotate. The placeholder phone number is
public by design.

### Verification after upgrade

- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `next build` static, 14.4 kB / 117 kB.
- Dev server reports **Next.js 15.5.25**, all requests 200, no build errors.
- Server-rendered HTML: **7 images**, all **9 section headings** present.
- Live DOM: **19 `tel:` links, 0 missing `data-call-cta`**, 58 reveals armed,
  Lenis active, headline highlight intact, no horizontal overflow.

Pushed as `332cdc4`; local and `origin/main` in sync.

